sceneDescription:
Franziska, a brown-eyed adult woman with dark brown hair slicked back into a bun, her oval face framed by prominent cheekbones and a soft jawline, dressed in a white and blue floral print v-neck midi dress and brown sandals, sets down a heavy dark-green cotton shopping net with a red rim onto the grey granite cobblestones of the narrow old-town street with a decisive thud — the net bulging with carrots poking from the top and a chicken package nestled inside, the rope handles stretched taut from the weight. She stands on the left side of the scene, her gaze fixed directly at Lukas, her expression focused and clear. Lukas, a slim grade-school boy with short straight brown hair parted to the right, brown eyes, and rounded childish features, sits on a chair to the right in the midground, looking up at her from below, his head tilted back slightly to meet her eyes — he wears a blue and light-blue striped short-sleeve t-shirt, dark blue shorts, and green and black flip-flops. Afternoon sunlight pours down from above, casting sharp shadows from the old weathered stone wall on the left across the uneven cobblestones, while the creamand ochre-coloured buildings of the Altstadtgasse recede into the bright distance behind them. Medium shot capturing the moment of silent communication between mother and son on the quiet street.

